haikuwebkit 1.10.0: cross-compiling, and JavaScriptCore on Haiku arm64

The Haiku port of WebKit has only been built natively, and for x86 and x86_64 so far:
- WebCore, WebKitLegacy: the private netservices headers from the sysroot (CMAKE_SYSROOT is empty
  in a native build, and /boot/system is /system there)
- MachineContext.h: the arm64 registers in Haiku's mcontext_t (struct vregs: x[0..29], lr, sp, elr),
  as on FreeBSD; the conservative GC (thread suspension) needs the stack pointer even without JIT
- ARM64Assembler::cacheFlush(): libgcc's __clear_cache (dc cvau/ic ivau from user mode)
- offlineasm arm64.rb: globaladdr with ELF GOT relocations, as on Linux

